  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Structuring the Application**\n\nI\'m currently focused on structuring the application in a modular and organized way. I\'ve begun defining the feature structure and file organization. For now, I\'m focusing on defining core types, such as the `Category` type including properties like `id`, `name`, `color`, `icon`, and `description`. I\'ve also identified a couple of default categories.\n\n\n**Defining Activity Types**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining the data structures for activities. I\'ve outlined a `StatusPendaftaran` type, including states like \'BELUM_DAFTAR\', and \'SELESAI\'. I\'m also fleshing out the `Activity` type, which will include fields for titles, deadlines, details, URLs for submissions and documents, the year, and an organizer field. I\'m focusing on defining properties and their type. I\'m currently adding tags to the activity definition.\n\n\n**Populating Default Data**\n\nI\'m now populating the application with rich, default data in Indonesian. This includes examples of competitions and programs, such as the \"Youth Action Forum 5.0\" and \"National Business Plan Competition 2026\", to make the dashboard immediately look populated. I\'m focusing on providing high-quality real examples, covering various categories and statuses.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Creating the Initial Structure**\n\nI\'ve moved on to `/src/data/prismaSchema.ts` and `/src/data/nextjsStructure.ts`. I am preparing the exact `schema.prisma` code for Prisma + Supabase/PostgreSQL. I\'m also preparing the exact Next.js (App Router) folder structure and code snippets for API routes and Server Components. I\'m focused on the basic code, e.g., `app/page.tsx`, `app/activities/page.tsx`, `app/api/activities/route.ts`, and `prisma/schema.prisma`.\n\n\n**Developing UI Components**\n\nNow, I\'m working on the UI components. I\'m focusing on the `Navbar` with the application title, year filter, action buttons, and view toggles. Then, I am going to make `StatCards` for key metrics. I will also develop the `AnalyticsCharts` for category distribution, status breakdowns, and the `UpcomingDeadlines` component to list deadlines and provide status actions. Finally, I will write the `utils/storage.ts` module.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive components. I\'m building a modal dialog for creating and editing activities, incorporating validation, Indonesian labels, and selectors for categories and statuses. I\'m also developing a responsive table with multi-filter controls, sort options, and action buttons. Finally, I\'m constructing a detailed drawer/modal for viewing activity details and a modal for managing categories.\n\n\n**Implementing the Code Viewer**\n\nI\'m now implementing the interactive code viewer component, focusing on providing a comprehensive code-viewing experience. I\'m prioritizing the display of the complete Prisma Schema, the Next.js App Router folder structure, and the code for Server Components and API routes. I\'m making sure to include syntax highlighting and a handy button for easily copying the code.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 14
      nanos: 565202451
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
